arguments.prompt:
You are working in /tmp/sv-8c560c49cc7f403c96a034f4ed514d59/UniversityCourseCatalog — a .NET 8 Blazor Web App (Server interactivity) created with `dotnet new blazor`. The project already has Bootstrap CSS, a MainLayout, and the standard Blazor scaffolding.

Your task: Build a university course catalog application with the following features:
1. Browse departments and courses in a searchable, filterable list
2. View course detail pages (description, schedule, credits, instructor bio)
3. Students submit an enrollment request form (name, student ID, course selection) — standard HTML form, no wizards or real-time validation
4. Homepage shows featured courses and department links
5. No authentication
6. Hosted on university intranet (fast connectivity, so Server interactivity is fine)

Here's what to do:

## 1. Create Models (Models/ directory)

Create `Models/Department.cs`:
```csharp
namespace UniversityCourseCatalog.Models;

public class Department
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Name { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Code { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
```

Create `Models/Course.cs`:
```csharp
namespace UniversityCourseCatalog.Models;

public class Course
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Title { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Code { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public int Credits { get; set; }
    public string Schedule { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string InstructorName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string InstructorBio { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public int DepartmentId { get; set; }
    public string DepartmentName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public bool IsFeatured { get; set; }
}
```

Create `Models/EnrollmentRequest.cs`:
```csharp
using System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations;

namespace UniversityCourseCatalog.Models;

public class EnrollmentRequest
{
    [Required(ErrorMessage = "Name is required.")]
    [StringLength(100, ErrorMessage = "Name cannot exceed 100 characters.")]
    public string StudentName { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Required(ErrorMessage = "Student ID is required.")]
    [RegularExpression(@"^[A-Z]{2}\d{6}$", ErrorMessage = "Student ID must be in format: XX000000 (2 letters followed by 6 digits).")]
    public string StudentId { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Required(ErrorMessage = "Please select a course.")]
    [Range(1, int.MaxValue, ErrorMessage = "Please select a course.")]
    public int CourseId { get; set; }
}
```

## 2. Create Data Service (Services/ directory)

Create `Services/ICatalogService.cs`:
```csharp
using UniversityCourseCatalog.Models;

namespace UniversityCourseCatalog.Services;

public interface ICatalogService
{
    List<Department> GetDepartments();
    Department? GetDepartment(int id);
    List<Course> GetCourses(string? searchTerm = null, int? departmentId = null);
    List<Course> GetFeaturedCourses();
    Course? GetCourse(int id);
    bool SubmitEnrollmentRequest(EnrollmentRequest request);
}
```

Create `Services/CatalogService.cs` with an in-memory implementation that has seed data:
- At least 4 departments (Computer Science, Mathematics, Physics, English)
- At least 3 courses per department with realistic data
- Some courses marked as featured
- The service implements search by title/code and filter by department
- SubmitEnrollmentRequest just validates the course exists and returns true

## 3. Register service in Program.cs

Add `builder.Services.AddSingleton<ICatalogService, CatalogService>();` and the using for the Services namespace.

## 4. Create Pages

### Update the NavMenu (Components/Layout/NavMenu.razor)
Replace with a navigation that has: Home, Courses, Departments, Enroll links. Keep Bootstrap styling.

### Homepage (Components/Pages/Home.razor)
- Shows a hero banner with university name
- Featured courses section (cards with title, department, credits, link to detail)
- Department quick links section

### Courses page (Components/Pages/Courses.razor) at route "/courses"
- Search input (text box for search term)
- Department filter dropdown
- Displays matching courses in a card/table layout
- Each course links to its detail page
- Use interactive server rendering for search/filter

### Course Detail page (Components/Pages/CourseDetail.razor) at route "/courses/{id:int}"
- Shows full course info: title, code, description, credits, schedule, department
- Instructor section with name and bio
- Link to enroll

### Departments page (Components/Pages/Departments.razor) at route "/departments"
- Lists all departments with description
- Each links to courses page filtered by that department

### Enrollment page (Components/Pages/Enroll.razor) at route "/enroll"
- Standard EditForm with DataAnnotationsValidator
- Fields: Student Name, Student ID, Course dropdown (populated from service)
- Optional query parameter ?courseId to pre-select a course
- On successful submit, show a confirmation message
- Use interactive server rendering for form submission

## 5. Update app.css (wwwroot/app.css)
Add some custom styles for the hero banner and course cards to make it look like a university site. Keep it minimal but professional.

## Important implementation notes:
- Pages that need interactivity (Courses search/filter, Enroll form) should use `@rendermode InteractiveServer`
- Static pages (Home, Departments, CourseDetail) can use default static SSR
- Use `@inject ICatalogService CatalogService` to access data
- Use Bootstrap classes for layout and styling
- Keep the code clean and well-organized

Build all files, then run `dotnet build` to verify it compiles successfully.

